  "question": {
    "text": "If the shortest distance between the straight lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>38</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the integral value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math> is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Xl36N",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
